[docs-vocabulary
  [doc [#
docs-src/site/vocabulary.cxd — the one vocabulary, as data (RULED: DOCS-51 §1
and §5, PLAY-2, RS-1).

Read by scripts/gen_site/docs_vocabulary_check.cx (`make docs-vocabulary-check`,
TEST_TARGETS), the docs-vocabulary step, in the voice ratchet's shape
(voice.cxd): the site uses the rings' and the delivery grammar's words —
data, code, a query is a program over data, two rings and the groups above
them, decision / merge / step / run — and this file names the words it does
not use ([words]) and, per served source and word, the mentions it still
carries and why ([allow]).

  [words]   one [word] per word the site does not use: `id=` names it in a
            row, `rx=` is the pattern (RE2 syntax; `flags=` prefixes it,
            `(?i)` unless said), `scope=` limits it to the paths carrying that
            substring, `say=` is how the step names it, `spans=keep` counts inside
            code spans too (a label the playground's script spells).
  [tree]    the tree's own prose (RULED: WORDS-1): `words=` names the
            [word] ids also held over the files its [glob path=…] rows match —
            the Makefile, flows/, scripts/, the approved specs and the root
            rule files — with the same exemptions and the same [allow] rows.
  [allow]   one [page] per file and word: a file with no row for a word must
            read ZERO of it; a file with a row may read at most its `allow=`,
            and when it reads LESS the step refuses too, naming the new count,
            so the number here is always the measured one and only ever moves
            down. `why=` says which sense the mention is (a pipe's stage, a
            page recording that a word left) or which voice wave lowers the
            row to zero (`wave=`, as voice.cxd's floors).

Code spans are not prose: the step counts a word only outside a fenced
block, an inline `…` span, an HTML <code> span, a [fixture id=…] citation
and a path literal (a token
with a "/" ending in "/" or a file extension), so a directory, file or make
target named with a word keeps its spelling there and nowhere else. The
grammar's "green/red" and "job/stage/task" are scanned (2026-09-29): a mention
in another sense — a pipe's stage, a `job` element in a data example — is
an [allow] row whose why= names that sense, at its measured count, which
never rises. Not scanned, by name: "landing" ("landing page").
#]]

  [words
    [word id=ring-2-3 rx='\bring[ -][23]\b' say='"Ring 2" / "Ring 3"']
    [word id=ecosystem-ring rx='\becosystem rings?\b' say='"ecosystem ring"']
    [word id=monorepo rx='\bmonorepos?\b' say='"monorepo"']
    [word id=lane rx='\blanes?\b' say='"lane"']
    [word id=campaign rx='\bcampaigns?\b' say='"campaign"']
    [word id=gate-run rx='\bgate runs?\b' say='"gate run"']
    [word id=steward rx='\bstewards?\b' say='"steward"']
    [word id=ruling rx='\brulings?\b' say='"ruling"']
    [word id=landed rx='\blanded\b' say='"landed"']
    [; the owner, 2026-09-29: "take out TL;DR from the docs... its way overused" (RULED: DOCS-51 §1 and §7, DOCS-43): a page opens on its one-sentence lead as plain prose, never behind the label — a heading, a bold prefix or a rendered block title. A code span keeps its spelling, as for every word ]
    [word id=tldr rx='\btl;dr\b' say='the label "TL;DR"']
    [; the delivery grammar's verdict and unit words (RULED: DG-1, DOCS-51 §1; the owner, 2026-09-29: "we stick with our terminology"): a run passes or
       fails, and its units are steps in a pipeline — never green/red as a verdict, never a
       job, stage or task. An ordinary-English or language sense (a pipe's stage, a `job`
       element in a data example, the colour red) stays only as an [allow] row with its why= ]
    [word id=green-red rx='\b(green|red)\b' say='"green" / "red"']
    [word id=job rx='\bjobs?\b' say='"job"']
    [word id=stage rx='\bstages?\b' say='"stage"']
    [word id=task rx='\btasks?\b' say='"task"']
    [; the playground's readings are data / code (PLAY-3, amending PLAY-2's
       three, #1741): the old names may not come back as a tab or crumb
       label — a quoted string or element text reading exactly Document,
       Program or Query ]
    [word id=reading-label rx="(>|['\"])(Document|Program|Query)(<|['\"])" flags='' scope='playground' spans=keep say='the reading label "Document" / "Program" / "Query"']]

  [; ── the tree's own prose (RULED: WORDS-1, Letter 120 = (a)): the words named
     in `words=` are held over the tooling and process prose of the tree as well
     as over the served sources above — the Makefile, flows/, scripts/, the
     approved specs and the three root rule files — in the same shape: code
     spans, path literals and [fixture id=…] citations are exempt, a file with
     no [allow] row for the word reads zero of it, and a row's count only
     moves down. A file the served GLOBS already read is graded there, once.
     Not scanned, by name: ledger/ and the git history, which are records. ── ]
  [tree words='lane'
    [glob path='Makefile']
    [glob path='flows/**/*.cx'] [glob path='flows/**/*.cxd'] [glob path='flows/**/*.mk']
    [glob path='scripts/**/*.cx'] [glob path='scripts/**/*.sh']
    [glob path='spec/03-approved/**/*.md']
    [glob path='AGENTS.md'] [glob path='AGENT-STANDING-RULES.md'] [glob path='CONTRIBUTING.md']]

  [; ── the allowances, measured on the PLAY-2 tree and re-measured 2026-09-29: no served row for lane, campaign, gate run or steward (the tree's lane rows, WORDS-1's, close the list); rows with wave= are floors the voice pass lowers ── ]
  [allow
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/01a-rings.cxd" word=ring-2-3 allow=2 why="the page records, in its file comment and prose, that Ring 2 and Ring 3 left under RS-1 and that no such ring exists"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/00-quickstart.cxd" word=stage allow=1 why="the `[?pipe]` stage — the code language's own word for one transform of a pipe (code.md §6.4, §8.9), not a pipeline unit"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/05-analytics.cxd" word=stage allow=3 why="a stage of a streaming pipe — the code language's word for one transform a row group flows through, not a pipeline unit"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/06-code.cxd" word=stage allow=15 why="the `[?pipe]` stage — the code language's own word for one transform of a pipe (code.md §6.4, §8.9), not a pipeline unit"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/08-tooling.cxd" word=job allow=1 why="a CI service's own `jobs:` key inside the workflow-file example"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/12-faq.cxd" word=stage allow=3 why="the `[?pipe]` stage — the code language's own word for one transform of a pipe (code.md §6.4, §8.9), not a pipeline unit"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/14-tour-data.cxd" word=green-red allow=1 why="the colour, in the tour's text-body example (\"Roses are red\")"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/15-tour-programs.cxd" word=stage allow=1 why="the `[?pipe]` stage — the code language's own word for one transform of a pipe (code.md §6.4, §8.9), not a pipeline unit"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/16a-code-tooling.cxd" word=stage allow=1 why="the `[?pipe]` stage — the code language's own word for one transform of a pipe (code.md §6.4, §8.9), not a pipeline unit"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/19-xap-distribution.cxd" word=stage allow=12 why="the registry's growth stages (stage 1 a git registry, stage 2 served) — xap_dist.md's own term, not a pipeline unit"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/05a-data-tooling.cxd" word=ruling allow=1 wave=5 why="the grammar's word is decision; the voice pass re-words it"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/06c-runtime-representation.cxd" word=ruling allow=1 wave=5 why="the grammar's word is decision; the voice pass re-words it"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/17-operations.cxd" word=landed allow=1 wave=5 why="the grammar's word is merged; the voice pass re-words it"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/18-store.cxd" word=landed allow=1 wave=5 why="the grammar's word is merged; the voice pass re-words it"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/19-xap-distribution.cxd" word=landed allow=1 wave=5 why="the grammar's word is merged; the voice pass re-words it"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/sections/19a-ux-capability.cxd" word=ruling allow=2 wave=5 why="the grammar's word is decision; the voice pass re-words it"]
    [page path="docs-src/canonical/about.html" word=landed allow=1 why="hand-authored by the owner; the everyday sense (landed on an approach)"]
    [page path="docs-src/repos/cx-decisions.cxd" word=ruling allow=3 wave=5 why="the repository documents the ledger, whose pages are named rulings_<date>; the grammar's word is decision"]
